Recommends: cron | systemd
Suggests: unattended-upgrades
Description: automated Ubuntu/Debian server maintenance tool
 A production-ready command-line utility for automated Ubuntu/Debian
 server maintenance. Provides safe, logged, and auditable system updates
 with multiple operation modes.
 .
 Features:
  * Multiple update modes: force (with reboot), all (no reboot), critical only
  * Dry-run mode for safe preview before applying changes
  * Comprehensive logging to /var/log/system_update.log
  * Safe reboots with 5-minute cancellation window
  * Interactive menu and command-line interface
  * Suitable for web servers, databases, and production environments
 .
 Security hardening includes: memory leak fixes, buffer overflow protection,
 input validation, comprehensive error handling, and audit logging.
